A||||22||Taijiguy||Super special custom theft deterrant very loud alarm systems anyone????||||3||
Z||000000||Taijiguy||08-12-2000||07:58 AM||||How about a thread here where we share our ideas on how to protect our prized little Fieros from being taken from us by some lowlife? What kind of alarm system do you have? Have you implimented any ingeneous little devices or add-ons to help prevent the theft? Here's what I did:<P>I have two sirens on my baby. One out under the hood (although I may move it to the back under the right side engine grill) and another siren INSIDE the passenger compartment. Even if the thief could withstand the sound of the siren going off in his ear (it's well concealed) he has to locate the controller. And even if he did, it wouldn't do him any good, since I have an ignition cutoff relay, and a seperate "carjack" switch (which I use in addition to the alarm system) that kills the fuel pump. The beauty of the carjack switch is, with the conversion to a carburetor, I kill the switch, the guy has enough gas to get him about 200 feet, and then the car dies. No gas. He runs away, I walk over to my car press the right buttons, let the pump re-prime the carb, and drive off! (Hopefully)<P>Anyone else have anything they don't mind sharing?<P>-Taiji<P>"If adversity creates depth, I'm the Atlantic Ocean!"||||reg||3
Z||000001||Cooter||08-12-2000||11:31 AM||||A while back I saw a pretty neat car alarm. It was a cute, cuddley Teddy Bear that just sat in the passenger seat. However, built into the bear was motion and sound sensors that would set off a monster loud alarm inside the bear if not properly disarmed. To prevent the would be bandit from just throwing it out the window, it had a steel cable that you bolted down with a seat bolt to keep him in place. It was fairly cheap too. Kind of like Teddy Ruxpin with an attitude!<P>------------------<BR>The slower they think you are, the more suprised they will be when you smoke them.||||reg||1
Z||000002||86SE||08-12-2000||02:46 PM||||I just have 2 door locks and a anti-theft switch hidden under the dash.  Flip the switch and it shuts off power the the fuel pump and the car does not even start.<P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero<BR>**Special Rally Heavy Duty Suspention**||||reg||1
Z||000003||Philphine||08-12-2000||05:42 PM||||i kind of considered making a "dead mans switch". some thing like a wire loop that is part of the ignition and/or fuel circuit. some thing like plug it in as the compleation of a circuit with maybe a velcro strap for your ankle. you get pulled out of the car, it pulls the wire and kills the pump or ignition system. but i've never felt so threatened to work on it. might be worth trying though.||||reg||1
Z||000004||My7Fieros||08-12-2000||10:22 PM||||I just pull the fuse to the fuel pump. Unless some dumba$$ decides he wants to steal my car (God help anyone if they do), he better have a set of fuses on him.<BR>Its actually funny that this topic came up. When I got my first Fiero, I got the idea to do that. The next time I went to start it, it wouldnt start....it drove me crazy, I FORGOT ABOUT TAKING THE FUSE OUT!!! DUH!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> Imagine how stupid (and relieved) I felt when I realized what was wrong!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 08-12-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 08-12-2000).]||||reg||12
