Z||000007||Oreif||08-13-2000||02:29 AM||||I want to get an alarm like the one in RoboCop 2. It's called "Magnavolt". It uses a high current/high voltage system to fry potential theives. According to the ad it won't even drain your battery!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||pHoOl||08-13-2000||11:52 PM||||well, i have a $20 alarm that i bought at radio shack.  loud, annoying, sensitive.  pretty good for $20.  btw, i was thinking of making a kill switch and making the switch in the ash tray.  so you'd have to flip up the black part and then hit the switch.  as im'm thinking about it, maybe put it under the tray so you'd have to open it up, then remove the tray, then hit the switch.  I'm getting carried away, anyway, what's the best spot in the circuit to hook it up to?  I've heard a lot of people doing fuel pump.  Is it easy to do?  I know how to solder and my dad's an electrical engineer, so i think we could figure it out, but i don't want to have to dig the car apart to do it.  any thoughts?<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Homicidal||08-14-2000||02:28 AM||||The ULTIMATE KILL switchs:<P>If the robber activates the kill switch while in the car (motion sensors play a part there) than the car will simply explode!  Viola, the ULTIMATE in theft deterrent!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
