Z||000011||86SE||08-14-2000||04:38 AM||||Just make it voice controlled with simple windows software.  If it recignises your voice, or other pre-programmed voices, it activates your fuelpump, or starter or what ever it may be.......just a thought||||reg||1
Z||000012||batboy||08-15-2000||04:25 PM||||My theft prevention plan. Live in the middle of nowhere in Kansas where crime is nonexistant. I have neighbors that still leave their keys in the ignition all the time. The other day, I went to work and left the door standing wide open (the outer screen door was closed). I didn't even bother to check and see if anything was damaged or missing because I knew nothing would be wrong. My itty-bitty town might be boring and quiet, but I like it that way.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Greg Piet||08-16-2000||03:43 PM||||Im partial to the security system from Mad Max.  Go ahead steal my car, but it will blow up and it will blow the thief up too.   If I cant have my car no one can!<P>If more cars had that there would be less car thiefs (and less cars I suppose)!||||reg||1
Z||000014||Taijiguy||08-16-2000||05:17 PM||||I saw a TV show once that had a feature on this anti-carjacking system, that consisted of flamethrowers on the sides of the car! The driver pressed and held a switch similar to a dimmer switch for like, 2 seconds, and the throwers would kick in and set the would-be thief on FIRE! This is a system that's actually available in Africa (I think) it was great! <BR>They had a "Security System" like you guys have been talking about on a James Bond movie once- on a Lotus Eprit. Thet bad guy busted out the window and the car exploded. The ULTIMATE car alarm. WOuld certainly cut back on thefts I think if you could really do that.....<P>-Taiji||||reg||1
